&= \mathop{\mathrm{E}}\p*{Y^2 \mid W} - \left\{ * \right\}{\mathop{\mathrm{E}}\p*{Y \mid W}}^2              && \text{ the \emph{excess} idea: the average amount $Y^2$ exceeds the square of its cond. mean}
\end{aligned}
}











We can think of the Conditional Variance as excess, too.
